  <h2 id="tech-heading">Technical Integration & Database Time Handling</h2>
  <p>
    When engineering software systems for cross-Atlantic usage between Portugal and Eastern North America, database timestamps must be handled with care. Standard practice dictates storing all UTC timestamps in ISO-8601 format (`2026-07-30T12:00:00Z`). When formatting timestamps for client user interfaces in Lisbon or New York, use the standardized IANA time zone identifiers:
  </p>
  <ul style="color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 1rem;">
    <li><code>Europe/Lisbon</code> – Controls Lisbon, Porto, and mainland Portugal transitions.</li>
    <li><code>Atlantic/Madeira</code> – Controls Madeira island daylight savings rules.</li>
    <li><code>Atlantic/Canary</code> – Controls Canary Islands (Spain) local rules.</li>
    <li><code>America/New_York</code> – Controls US Eastern Time rules.</li>
  </ul>
